From 421b46488b58f5b386860d5374a43c83fbe58ce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:16:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: a video at its own rate with VRR is paced
 whatever way its renderer takes, and VRR that does not come on changes the
 mode

"Video at its own rate with VRR" kept the mode of the menus and never
turned VRR on with Kodi's GLES renderer, the one that VAAPI goes through
on NVIDIA and AMD: PaceVrrVideo() paced a flip only with the video layer
(CApplicationPlayer::IsRenderingVideoLayer(), the renderer's
VideoBypassesFramebuffer()), which is true only for a renderer that gives
the video a DRM plane of its own; CLinuxRendererGLES says false whatever
IsGuiLayer() says. On an RTX 4080 SUPER with an LG C5 a
23.976 fps SDR video went at a fixed 120 Hz in the mode of the menus, and
kodi.log said only that it went "at its own rate".

- A flip is paced where a video is on its way to the screen
  (CApplicationPlayer::IsRenderingVideo(), paused or not) in the
  full-screen video (VRR_VIDEO::Paced()).
- Whether VRR came on is measured in the first second of each video
  (VRR_VIDEO::CStartCheck): VRR_ENABLED read back from the kernel, and the
  vblanks of the CRTC between the flips. With VRR on there is one a flip,
  at the time asked for; with a fixed refresh a flip waits for the next
  refresh of the mode (2 or 3 vblanks a flip at 47.952 Hz in a mode of
  120 Hz). Where it did not come on, or could not be measured in 5 s, the
  mode changes to the video's rate as without the setting (the render
  manager chooses it again), until no video has been on its way to the
  screen for 3 s; an INFO line in kodi.log says what was measured. The
  EDID cannot say it: the LG C5 declares HDMI VRR from 40 to 120 Hz with
  its own VRR setting off (no AMD FreeSync block in any of its EDIDs of
  the tests), and HDMI 2.1 gives a display no register that says whether
  it applies VRR.
- The player information says what became of it (hades.out.vrr:
  checking, follows, samerate, fixed), not what was asked for.
- The help says that the TV's own VRR setting must be on, that the TV
  does not tell, and what is checked.

New strings: Estuary 54300 to 54303, in English and in Spanish of Spain,
Argentina and Mexico; the help of the setting changed (62143, 54143).

The host test (tools/regress/kodi-host/vrr_video_test.cpp of LibreELEC
Hades) checks the chain of the GLES renderer, which the rule of 1.1 fails,
and the measure, and fails on each of 7 mutations of the header. Not
tried on a TV.
